WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:04.660
Welcome to the Science Asylum.

00:00:04.660 --> 00:00:06.520
I am Nick Lucid.

00:00:06.520 --> 00:00:08.800
I’ve noticed lately that I’ve had a lot of energy.

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:13.880
[Exercise Noises]

00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:16.920
It’s just bursting to get out of me and that got me thinking:

00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:19.500
What is energy? I mean, what is it really?!

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:24.600
The problem here stems from our limited ability to define things in our language.

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:30.560
So to deal with this problem, I started with the Online Etymology Dictionary to find the origin of the word itself,

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:35.520
which turned out to be Ancient Greek for “at work” suggesting only what I already knew:

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:37.800
Energy gives us the ability to do stuff.

00:00:37.809 --> 00:00:43.010
In fact, all the definitions in all the dictionaries and science books seem to have that same problem.

00:00:43.010 --> 00:00:46.000
They tell us what energy does, not what it is.

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:47.100
What is it?!

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:50.060
We really only have two ways of understanding things

00:00:50.060 --> 00:00:54.040
First, we could compare and contrast with something we already understand.

00:00:54.040 --> 00:00:57.380
or, second, we could divide it into parts and categorize them.

00:00:57.380 --> 00:01:01.160
Unfortunately, energy is unlike anything we’ve ever seen before

00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:03.720
and it appears to have no parts whatsoever,

00:01:03.720 --> 00:01:05.340
which leaves us in a bit of a pickle.

00:01:05.340 --> 00:01:06.500
Hmm.

00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:09.380
Wait, it does look different when it’s in different places.

00:01:09.380 --> 00:01:11.540
What? You’ve never seen energy before?

00:01:11.540 --> 00:01:13.740
That’s because you’re using your eyes.

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:15.500
You’ve got to use your mind’s eye.

00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:18.020
Go find your imagination and dust it off.

00:01:18.020 --> 00:01:19.380
Got it? Ok, cool.

00:01:19.380 --> 00:01:21.940
If we can find out all the places it can be,

00:01:21.940 --> 00:01:24.380
then maybe then we’ll have a better idea of what it is.

00:01:24.380 --> 00:01:25.460
Can we make a list?

00:01:25.460 --> 00:01:27.440
Definitely! I love lists.

00:01:27.440 --> 00:01:29.920
We've seen stuff nearby other stuff.

00:01:29.920 --> 00:01:31.480
We'll call that potential energy.

00:01:31.480 --> 00:01:33.040
We've seen stuff moving.

00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:34.740
We can call that kinetic energy.

00:01:34.740 --> 00:01:36.700
We've felt stuff be really warm.

00:01:36.700 --> 00:01:38.440
We can call that thermal energy.

00:01:38.440 --> 00:01:39.640
We've seen stuff shine.

00:01:39.640 --> 00:01:41.720
We can call that light energy, I guess.

00:01:41.720 --> 00:01:45.920
And stuff explodes too, which has to do with chemical and nuclear energy.

00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:47.540
Oh! And, uh, life is a thing.

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:50.260
I mean, our bodies are just chemical energy machines, right?

00:01:50.260 --> 00:01:52.240
You know what might be even better for this than a list?

00:01:52.240 --> 00:01:53.640
A concept tree!

00:01:53.640 --> 00:01:57.160
Ok, let’s see, move this over here, move that over there, and voila!

00:01:57.160 --> 00:01:58.840
That’s a lot of different energies.

00:01:58.840 --> 00:02:01.340
No way is the universe really that complicated

00:02:01.340 --> 00:02:03.320
and what the heck is this stuff, anyway?!

00:02:03.320 --> 00:02:06.220
Internal energy is the energy inside stuff,

00:02:06.220 --> 00:02:08.980
so that must have something to do with the molecules making up the stuff.

00:02:08.980 --> 00:02:10.920
We need to imagine a little smaller.

00:02:10.920 --> 00:02:14.300
Molecules move, spin, and wiggle, so that’s just kinetic energy.

00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:16.220
They do have a tendency to stay together,

00:02:16.220 --> 00:02:20.060
but bounce off each other when they get too close. That’s potential energy.

00:02:20.060 --> 00:02:23.060
Chemical energy is what holds the atoms together in a molecule.

00:02:23.060 --> 00:02:24.800
Again, that’s potential energy.

00:02:24.800 --> 00:02:29.600
Nuclear energy is holding the atomic nucleus together, so that’s just potential energy too.

00:02:29.600 --> 00:02:31.240
Ok, this is looking a lot better.

00:02:31.240 --> 00:02:34.600
Everything is just potential energy, kinetic energy, or mass.

00:02:34.600 --> 00:02:35.920
So what’s mass?

00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:38.180
That’s not a simple question to answer fully,

00:02:38.180 --> 00:02:42.300
but the short version is that it depends on how you're looking at the stuff in question.

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:46.580
If you’re so close that you can see the quarks inside the protons,

00:02:46.580 --> 00:02:48.980
then it doesn’t look like there’s a whole lot of mass there.

00:02:48.980 --> 00:02:52.300
But, if we zoom out, it just looks like a single proton.

00:02:52.300 --> 00:02:57.660
All that potential energy holding the quarks together looks like mass because we really can’t see it anymore.

00:02:57.660 --> 00:03:00.800
The point is that almost all the energy we call “mass"

00:03:00.800 --> 00:03:04.000
is just the potential energy in the nuclei of the atoms.

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:05.740
You're mostly just empty space.

00:03:05.740 --> 00:03:09.740
So, in the end, energy is really just potential energy and kinetic energy,

00:03:09.740 --> 00:03:13.360
some of it just happens to be in the tiny nooks and crannies inside things.

00:03:13.360 --> 00:03:15.560
This hasn’t really answer our question yet.

00:03:15.560 --> 00:03:17.020
No, I guess it hasn’t. Huh.

00:03:17.020 --> 00:03:19.700
On top of that, kinetic energy is kind of weird.

00:03:19.700 --> 00:03:22.340
I mean, the driver of a car has kinetic energy, right?

00:03:22.340 --> 00:03:24.600
Well, what if you’re a passenger in that same car?

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:26.820
As far as you’re concerned the driver is sitting still.

00:03:26.820 --> 00:03:29.720
No no, the Earth is stationary and we’re both moving.

00:03:29.720 --> 00:03:31.280
The Earth is stationary?

00:03:31.280 --> 00:03:33.220
What about it rotating once a day?

00:03:33.220 --> 00:03:35.240
Or going around the Sun once a year?

00:03:35.240 --> 00:03:38.000
Or zipping around the center of the galaxy with the Sun?

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:40.840
So yeah, this leaves us with an unfortunate truth.

00:03:40.840 --> 00:03:43.040
We don’t really know what energy is.

00:03:43.040 --> 00:03:48.460
Every hypothesis we've ever had that has pretended it’s some kind of substance has epically failed.

00:03:48.460 --> 00:03:52.360
It seems to only be this weird abstract property of the universe.

00:03:52.360 --> 00:03:56.200
Energy is just a number and the total amount never changes.

00:03:56.200 --> 00:03:58.200
So, what do you do when you have a lot of energy?

00:03:58.200 --> 00:03:59.800
Wink wink, nudge nudge.

00:03:59.800 --> 00:04:01.240
Please share in the comments.

00:04:01.240 --> 00:04:04.900
And until next time, remember, it’s ok to be a little crazy.

